  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "LASGZiROfIRlUQtZKkdqMvCNBuI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:07.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "# versioning operations on document models are not implemented\n\nThe document model operation taxonomy includes a \"Versioning\" category, but it is explicitly marked as not implemented. Do not use any versioning-related operations \u2014 they will fail or produce undefined behavior.\n\nThis is a known gap in these particular operations: in `packages/document-model/schemas/document-model/versioning.graphql` the four change-log inputs are declared as `type ...Input` rather than `input ...Input`, so no operations are generated from them at all.\n\nDocument-model versioning itself is *not* unsolved, though \u2014 it has first-class support through the document model registry's **upgrade manifests**, not git. Register them at build time with `ReactorBuilder.withUpgradeManifests(manifests)` or at runtime with `registerUpgradeManifests()`, then read them back with `getUpgradeManifest(documentType)`, `computeUpgradePath(documentType, from, to)`, and `getUpgradeReducer(documentType, from, from + 1)`. The registry keys modules by document type *and* version so multiple versions coexist, and each manifest describes the migration between consecutive versions.\n\n---\n\nTopics:\n- [[gotchas]]\n- [[architecture decisions]]\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:07.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:07.000Z"
    }
  },
